{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2151-06-07 22:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. You’re here because you’ve been vomiting blood. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2151-06-07 22:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had two episodes of vomiting blood in the last two days. It’s scary. I was just feeling better after my last hospital stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2151-06-07 22:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. You mentioned at the ER that you were recently diagnosed with lupus and started on steroids. Can you tell me more about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2151-06-07 22:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, at the other hospital they said my blood work suggested lupus, gave me IV steroids for five days, and sent me home on prednisone. I was feeling great until two days ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2151-06-07 22:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. And you’ve also had chronic abdominal pain and nausea for years. Did the prednisone help with that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2151-06-07 22:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It did, actually. For the first time in months, I wasn’t in pain. But now it’s back—same pain, nausea, and then the vomiting with blood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2151-06-07 22:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. We’ve checked your labs. Your hemoglobin is low at 10.7, but it’s stable. White blood cells are high, likely from the steroids. No sign of infection in your blood culture."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2151-06-07 22:57:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the blood in my vomit from an ulcer again? I had ulcers found on an EGD last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2151-06-07 22:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a possibility. We’ll schedule an EGD tomorrow to look inside. For now, we’re giving you IV fluids and continuing your prednisone. We’ve also restarted your Nexium to protect your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2151-06-07 22:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I also have this cold—sore throat, runny nose. I was on Augmentin, but it made me nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2151-06-07 23:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw you were on antibiotics. Since your symptoms are mild and it’s likely a viral URI, we’ll stop the Augmentin. We don’t want to irritate your stomach more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2151-06-07 23:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2151-06-08 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2151-06-08 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still nauseous, and I had another episode of vomiting, but no blood this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2151-06-08 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good—no fresh bleeding. Your labs are stable. We’re going to do the EGD today to check for ulcers or other causes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2151-06-08 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will they put me to sleep for it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2151-06-08 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll be sedated. It’s routine. They’ll also take a small biopsy from your duodenum, since you have a history of malabsorption."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2151-06-08 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2151-06-08 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from the EGD. The good news is no active bleeding. They saw a small hiatal hernia and some atrophy in the duodenum. Biopsies were taken."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2151-06-08 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No ulcers? But I had them before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2151-06-08 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No new ulcers. The previous ones may have healed. The bleeding might be from a small tear in the esophagus from vomiting—called a Mallory-Weiss tear. It often stops on its own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2151-06-08 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I’ve heard of that. So it’s not serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2151-06-08 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not usually. Since your hemoglobin isn’t dropping, we’ll monitor you and keep you on stomach-protecting meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2151-06-08 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2151-06-09 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You tolerated a soft diet yesterday without vomiting. How’s your pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2151-06-09 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Still there, but not as bad. I’m glad I could eat something."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2151-06-09 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We did an abdominal X-ray yesterday. No blockage, but there’s a lot of stool in your colon. That could be contributing to your discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2151-06-09 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been constipated since the pain started. I’m not moving much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2151-06-09 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start a gentle laxative—senna—and docusate to help. Staying regular will help your gut feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2151-06-09 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2151-06-09 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your rheumatology workup came back. Most markers are normal. No clear evidence of active lupus here, but we’ll continue your prednisone as started."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2151-06-09 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But the other doctor said I have lupus. I’m confused."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2151-06-09 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s confusing. Sometimes diagnoses are made based on symptoms and limited tests. Here, your ANA and other markers are normal. But since you were started on treatment, we don’t stop it abruptly. Your PCP will help decide next steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2151-06-09 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll follow up with her."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. No more vomiting, pain is controlled. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue prednisone, but at a lower dose—20 mg daily. We’re switching from 60 mg. Don’t stop it suddenly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know, I’ve been on it before. What about the stomach medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll stay on esomeprazole twice daily. We’re also adding sucralfate four times a day to coat and protect your stomach lining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And for nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you Zofran tablets that dissolve under the tongue. Use them as needed for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I like those."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also adjusting your amitriptyline—from 50 mg to 25 mg at bedtime. It may help with pain and sleep but with fewer side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ve had dry mouth on it before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This dose might help. And keep taking your fludrocortisone and betaxolol for POTS."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had dizziness, so that’s good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Your condition is stable. No active bleeding, pain is manageable, and you’re eating well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I was worried about the bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. The EGD was reassuring. Keep taking your meds, especially the prednisone. Follow up with your PCP within a week to discuss continuing cellcept if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll call for my biopsy results from the EGD?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your GI doctor will contact you about those. If you vomit blood again, go to the ER. Otherwise, you’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—should I be worried about Sjogren’s? I was told I might have it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You mentioned a positive tear test and salivary issues as a child. But no biopsy was done. Your PCP may want to pursue that, especially with your family history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, my dad’s side has lupus and Sjogren’s. I’ll bring it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good idea. For now, focus on recovery. You’ve been through a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your discharge instructions and prescriptions. You can leave once that’s done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy. Rest, stay hydrated, and follow up as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope the prednisone keeps helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should, but your doctor will monitor for side effects and decide if long-term treatment is needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright, I’ll let the nurse know you’re ready for discharge paperwork."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2151-06-07 22:50:00",
    "admission_end": "2151-06-11 13:05:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of chronic abdominal pain, Sjogren’s syndrome, POTS, and recent lupus diagnosis presented with hematemesis and recurrent nausea and vomiting. She had been started on prednisone for presumed lupus at a prior admission and was feeling well until two days before this admission. In the hospital, she had no active bleeding, stable hemoglobin, and an EGD showed no source of hemorrhage, with findings of a small hiatal hernia and duodenal atrophy. The bleeding was likely due to a Mallory-Weiss tear. Her abdominal pain was managed with medications, and she was transitioned to oral intake. Her prednisone was continued at a reduced dose, and she was discharged home with instructions to follow up with her PCP regarding ongoing immunosuppressive therapy. A URI was treated by discontinuing Augmentin due to GI intolerance.",
    "problems": [
      "Hematemesis",
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Systemic lupus erythematosus",
      "Sicca syndrome",
      "Postural tachycardia syndrome",
      "Acute upper respiratory infections of unspecified site",
      "Unspecified intestinal malabsorption",
      "Glucocorticoid deficiency",
      "Von Willebrand's disease",
      "Dysthymic disorder"
    ]
  }
}
